course: dictionary
lesson: 6927
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pad is one of them. To know which meaning is right, read the words around it, which are its context. «Tell a grown-up about a blister and cover it with a plaster or blister pad.» Here a pad covers something to protect it, because a plaster and a blister pad are both for covering a wound.
explain: «When a baby tooth comes out, bite on clean gauze (a soft cloth pad) to stop the bleeding.» The bracket gives you a clue: the writer is telling you what gauze is, a soft cloth pad. So here a pad is a soft piece of material used to cover something.
explain: Pad can also be a block of paper, or a flat place. «Frogs sit on lily pads» tells you the pad is a flat place, because a frog sits on it. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means.
fact: «Pad» can mean a thick piece of soft material that protects you, such as «knee pads» or «wrist guards».
fact: «Pad» can mean a block of sheets of paper fixed together, like a notepad.
fact: «Pad» can mean the soft parts underneath an animal's paw, and «to pad» means to walk softly and quietly.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: In «bite on clean gauze (a soft cloth pad)», what does pad mean? | A flat area where rockets take off | A block of paper for writing notes | *A soft cloth used to cover or protect | To walk softly and quietly
exercise: «The cat padded across the room, silent as a shadow.» What does padded mean? | To write a note on a pad | To hop up high like a frog | *To walk softly and quietly | To fill something with soft material
exercise: «She tore a page from her pad to write a note.» What does pad mean in this sentence? | *A block of sheets of paper fixed together | A flat place for lily pads to float on | The soft part under an animal's paw | A thick cloth to fill a cushion
test: «Frogs sit on lily pads.» What does pad mean here? | A thick piece of soft material to protect | *A flat area, such as a leaf floating on water | To walk quietly | A block of paper
test: Which sentence uses pad to mean protection? | *«He wore knee pads when he skated.» | «She tore a page from her pad.» | «The cat's pads were soft.» | «The rocket left the launch pad.»
exam: In «Survivors had bigger toe pads that grip better», what does pad mean? | A block of sheets of paper | A flat place where rockets launch | *The soft parts underneath the toes that help a lizard grip | A thick cloth that fills a cushion
